  "reason": "First execution of -v1 (reports/validation/674-cumulative-candidate/review-836/graph-replay-v1-first-execution/report.json, a development run after one disclosed harness error) failed G7 and G9 on one observable each: old_refusal read 'tombstoned', the -v1 expectation said 'logical_memory_deleted'. The -v1 author copied the refusal token from the #777 pin, where the pruned memory is a two-version chain and the traversed node is its superseded first version (a deleted-lineage member); in these cases the pruned node is a single-version head, whose canonical refusal is 'tombstoned'. Both tokens are the recorded canonical refusal of a deleted node (docs/44: a governed-deleted generation is closed), which is what the clause requires. -v2 accepts either token on exactly those two observables and changes nothing else; no runtime behaviour was altered to obtain it. The nine other cases and the recorded G10 limitation were observed identically in that run."
